module BuilderExpansion

### BuilderExpansion is RazorForge's COMPTIME member-walk / generative-reflection surface — the sibling of
### the describe-only [BuilderQuery] module. Where BuilderQuery answers "what does this type look like?" at
### build time, BuilderExpansion LAYS DOWN CODE per member/case/arm of a type via the `expand` loop, folding
### the per-part handle projections to literals at monomorphization. (Suflae reflects at RUNTIME via
### ObjectHacker instead; this module is RF-only buildtime.)
###
### `import BuilderExpansion` is the opt-in that unlocks the `expand` construct and its reflection
### intrinsics. Like `import BuilderQuery`, it is a capability gate, not a symbol import: the intrinsics
### below are recognized by the compiler and FOLDED at build time (they have no runtime routine body — the
### per-part handle `m` is a buildtime-only value with no user-spellable type), so they are documented here
### rather than declared as callable routines.
###
### ── The loop (a keyword; the ONLY reflection keyword) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
###   `expand <m> in <source>(T)` — unroll the body once per part of T, binding `m` to each part.
###
### ── Sources (buildtime member/case/arm sets; the thing `expand` iterates) ──────────────────────────
###   `allmemvarof(T)`   — ALL member variables of a record/entity/tuple, declaration order (incl. secret).
###   `openmemvarof(T)`  — the OPEN ∪ POSTED (publicly readable) member variables only.
###   `caseof(T)`        — the cases of a `choice`/`flags`.
###   `branchof(T)`      — the arms of a `variant` (used inside a `when` to emit one clause per arm).
###
### ── Accessors (read a buildtime property off the active handle `m`, or a type) ──────────────────────
###   `nameof(m) -> Text`          — the member/case/arm name as declared.
###   `typeof(m) -> <typewise>`    — the member's type as a buildtime typewise receiver.
###   `typeidof(m) -> U64`         — the stable compile-time type id of the member's type.
###   `orderof(m) -> U64`          — the member's declaration index.
###   `placeof(m) -> U64`          — the member's byte offset in the type's layout.
###   `sizeof(T) -> U64`           — the byte size of a type.
###   `valueof(c) -> S32|U64`      — a case's computed value: a choice's S32 discriminant / a flags' U64 bit.
###   `visibilityof(m) -> Visibility` — the member's OPEN/POSTED/SECRET visibility (the BuilderQuery choice).
###
### Splice `$` weaves a handle projection into surface syntax: it binds to the immediately-following
### primary (an intrinsic call or identifier) and injects that buildtime value as code — `me.$nameof(m)`
### becomes a real member access at unroll, `$typeof(m)` a type argument / typewise receiver, `$valueof(c)`
### a case constant. See the Wiki (Expansion) for worked derives.
